WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.422 --> 00:00:16.753
That morning at school, Sara noticed a plump, blond girl about the same age as Sara.

2
00:00:17.914 --> 00:00:21.757
The girl was chewing on the ribbon of her pigtail and staring at Sara.

3
00:00:23.078 --> 00:00:27.302
When Monsieur Dufarge spoke to Sara, the plump girl looked a little frightened.

4
00:00:28.242 --> 00:00:32.777
When Sara replied in French, the girl gave a startled jump and turned red.

5
00:00:33.917 --> 00:00:37.438
Miss Minchin was still in a bad mood about Sara's perfect French.

6
00:00:37.458 --> 00:00:39.299
"Miss St.

7
00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:41.579
John, stop chewing on your ribbon!

8
00:00:42.279 --> 00:00:43.460
And sit up at once!"

9
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:44.660
she snapped.

10
00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:47.321
The girl gave another startled jump.

11
00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:51.842
Lavinia and Jessie giggled, and the girl turned redder than ever.

12
00:00:54.923 --> 00:00:57.784
Sara's father often remarked on Sara's soft heart.

13
00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:03.394
"Sara always wants to fight when she sees people in trouble," he liked to say.

14
00:01:04.555 --> 00:01:06.155
And that was certainly true now.

15
00:01:06.175 --> 00:01:12.238
"Those girls shouldn't laugh," thought Sara.

16
00:01:12.258 --> 00:01:13.819
"That's mean."

17
00:01:15.199 --> 00:01:20.461
But Lavinia and Jessie continued to snicker when the girl spoke in French for Monsieur Dufarge.

18
00:01:21.542 --> 00:01:26.124
Sara felt sorry for this girl, who had such trouble saying the French words correctly.

19
00:01:27.284 --> 00:01:30.167
The French lessons were obviously quite difficult for her.

20
00:01:31.748 --> 00:01:37.473
When the morning's lessons were finally finished, the plump girl sat on a window seat, looking miserable.

21
00:01:39.454 --> 00:01:40.695
Sara went over to her.

22
00:01:41.776 --> 00:01:42.597
"What's your name?"

23
00:01:43.117 --> 00:01:43.858
asked Sara.

24
00:01:44.699 --> 00:01:47.301
The girl seemed amazed that Sara was talking to her.

25
00:01:47.321 --> 00:01:50.083
"My name is Ermengarde St.

26
00:01:50.123 --> 00:01:51.584
John," she replied.

27
00:01:51.604 --> 00:01:56.572
"Mine is Sara Crewe.

28
00:01:56.592 --> 00:01:58.113
What a pretty name you have!"

29
00:01:58.634 --> 00:01:59.594
exclaimed Sara.

30
00:01:59.614 --> 00:02:02.617
"It sounds like a name from a story."

31
00:02:02.637 --> 00:02:04.918
"I like your name too.

32
00:02:05.719 --> 00:02:07.300
Where did you learn to speak French?"

33
00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:08.761
Ermengarde asked.

34
00:02:08.781 --> 00:02:13.084
"Oh, I've done it all my life," Sara answered.

35
00:02:13.104 --> 00:02:17.087
"If you'd always heard French at home, you could do it too."

36
00:02:17.107 --> 00:02:21.950
"No, I don't think so," said Ermengarde sadly.

37
00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:23.932
"I'm not very smart."

38
00:02:25.096 --> 00:02:28.558
Ermengarde explained that her father spoke seven or eight languages.

39
00:02:29.899 --> 00:02:35.903
He had a huge library filled with thousands of books and couldn't understand why Ermengarde didn't do well

40
00:02:35.943 --> 00:02:36.484
in school.

41
00:02:37.484 --> 00:02:40.647
He had told Miss Minchin that Ermengarde must be made to learn.

42
00:02:41.687 --> 00:02:45.130
But at school Ermengarde was often in trouble or in tears.

43
00:02:47.371 --> 00:02:48.972
"You're smart, aren't you?"

44
00:02:49.553 --> 00:02:50.773
Ermengarde said to Sara.

45
00:02:51.914 --> 00:02:54.336
Sara looked out the window into the dirty square.

46
00:02:55.536 --> 00:02:58.538
She could see some sparrows hopping along iron railings.

47
00:02:59.498 --> 00:03:00.499
She thought for a minute.

48
00:03:00.519 --> 00:03:03.000
"Oh, I don't know."

49
00:03:04.301 --> 00:03:06.202
Then suddenly she changed the subject.

50
00:03:06.222 --> 00:03:08.384
"Would you like to meet Emily?"

51
00:03:08.404 --> 00:03:10.245
"Who's Emily?"

52
00:03:10.725 --> 00:03:11.545
asked Ermengarde.

53
00:03:11.565 --> 00:03:15.628
"Come up to my room and see," replied Sara.

54
00:03:17.589 --> 00:03:19.450
Ermengarde followed Sara upstairs.

55
00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:25.226
"Is it true," she asked, "that you have a playroom all to yourself?"

56
00:03:26.967 --> 00:03:28.749
"Yes," Sara answered.

57
00:03:28.769 --> 00:03:31.671
"Papa asked Miss Minchin to let me have one.

58
00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:34.293
It's because I like to tell myself stories.

59
00:03:34.733 --> 00:03:37.676
And the mood gets spoiled if I know people are listening."

60
00:03:39.357 --> 00:03:41.459
Sara stopped outside the door to her room.

61
00:03:41.479 --> 00:03:47.404
"If we're quiet, maybe we'll catch her," she said mysteriously.

62
00:03:48.565 --> 00:03:49.505
Ermengarde blinked.

63
00:03:50.226 --> 00:03:52.468
She had no idea what Sara was talking about.

64
00:03:53.464 --> 00:03:55.325
But Sara's eyes were full of fun.

65
00:03:56.545 --> 00:03:58.465
Ermengarde couldn't wait to see what happened.

66
00:03:59.646 --> 00:04:01.046
Sara threw open the door.

67
00:04:03.927 --> 00:04:07.548
Ermengarde saw a beautiful doll sitting on a chair in front of the fire.

68
00:04:07.568 --> 00:04:11.289
"Oh, Emily is back in her seat!"

69
00:04:11.949 --> 00:04:13.370
Sara sounded disappointed.

70
00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.230
"Can she walk?"

71
00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.331
asked Ermengarde in surprise.

72
00:04:17.351 --> 00:04:21.988
"I like to pretend she can," said Sara.

73
00:04:22.008 --> 00:04:23.549
"Don't you pretend such things?"

74
00:04:23.569 --> 00:04:28.311
"No." Ermengarde was in awe of this strange girl.

75
00:04:28.331 --> 00:04:31.832
"Never. May I hold Emily?"

76
00:04:31.852 --> 00:04:35.354
"Of course," said Sara.

77
00:04:35.374 --> 00:04:37.354
"And I'll tell you stories."

78
00:04:38.835 --> 00:04:40.056
So they sat together.

79
00:04:40.596 --> 00:04:45.698
Her green eyes shining, Sara told Ermengarde all about the secret life of dolls.

80
00:04:46.778 --> 00:04:50.200
She also talked about life in India and the voyage to England.

81
00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:56.423
When Sara got to the part about finding Emily in the toy shop, she suddenly looked upset.

82
00:04:57.424 --> 00:05:00.806
Ermengarde had the feeling that Sara was bravely trying not to cry.

83
00:05:00.826 --> 00:05:02.848
"What's wrong?"

84
00:05:03.348 --> 00:05:04.329
she asked in alarm.

85
00:05:04.349 --> 00:05:08.772
"Do you love your father more than anything in the world?"

86
00:05:09.272 --> 00:05:10.213
Sara burst out.

87
00:05:11.073 --> 00:05:13.475
Ermengarde thought this was a strange question.

88
00:05:13.495 --> 00:05:15.997
"I hardly ever see him.

89
00:05:16.577 --> 00:05:18.879
He's always in his library reading things."

90
00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:23.705
"Oh, I love my father and miss him so."

91
00:05:24.545 --> 00:05:26.485
Sara buried her head in her hands.

92
00:05:27.906 --> 00:05:29.766
Ermengarde's mouth fell open a little.

93
00:05:30.847 --> 00:05:34.088
Sara was so wonderful and different from anyone else.

94
00:05:35.248 --> 00:05:36.408
Sara lifted her head.

95
00:05:36.428 --> 00:05:41.029
"If I keep telling you stories, I won't miss him as much."

96
00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:45.911
Tears came to Ermengarde's eyes, and she felt a lump in her throat.

97
00:05:45.931 --> 00:05:50.372
"Lavinia and Jessie are best friends.

98
00:05:51.152 --> 00:05:53.035
Do you think we could be best friends?

99
00:05:53.535 --> 00:05:55.898
You're so smart, and I'm not smart at all.

100
00:05:56.279 --> 00:05:57.760
But I like you very much!"

101
00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:02.967
"Of course we can be best friends," said Sara.

102
00:06:03.387 --> 00:06:04.409
Her face lit up.

103
00:06:04.429 --> 00:06:07.212
"And do you know what, Ermengarde?

104
00:06:07.893 --> 00:06:09.956
I can help you with your French lessons!"
